KG42.register("source_edge_archive-a9a71a4be7a4f9240ecdba74",{"id":"03-bilateral_p2p::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001","paper":"03-bilateral_p2p","rule_id":"v141-c-R004","rule_ref":"03-bilateral_p2p::v141-c-R004","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"matching.counterparties","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E26"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-535650ecb2e046e9","target":"COMP-844db09f135647e9","source_occurrence_id":"03-bilateral_p2p::v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","target_occurrence_id":"03-bilateral_p2p::v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties","source_unit_id":"03-bilateral_p2p::v141-a-M01::coordination.price_signal","target_unit_id":"03-bilateral_p2p::v141-a-M01::matching.counterparties","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"matching","context_text":"Contract-network topology used in case studies A and B. | Forward and real-time bilateral P2P markets; agents selecting contracts with potential counterparties. | Individual contract selection during each iteration of the forward and real-time price-adjustment process. | Initialization of the price-adjustment process in each forward and real-time market; all agents. | Permitted extensions of the proposed bilateral P2P methodology beyond the illustrated case-study topology. | Potential counterparty relationships in the forward and real-time bilateral contract networks.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E26"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"f1af3eeb6bed4081f2e1567dd76c591439312d0753e1ef81f1a7456883ea2f5f","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Initialize trade buyer/seller prices to zero; for a buyer-selected seller-rejected trade increase the appropriate buyer or seller price by the minimum increment according to their ordering. Stop when no prices change. Preserve forward and real-time contexts.","target_definition":"Agents choose utility-maximizing upstream/downstream contract bundles from available menus; accepted/rejected contracts guide distributed price adjustments. Stable outcomes require full substitutability. Forward and real-time contracts and case topology remain separate variants.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The distributed price-adjustment process coordinates buyers' offers and sellers' acceptance or rejection to find an agreed bilateral contract network that the agents do not wish to mutually deviate from. Scope: Forward and real-time bilateral P2P markets; agents selecting contracts with potential counterparties. Condition: Agent preferences satisfy full substitutability.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E26"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E19","location":{"location_id":"src-4a31f0141b-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":"2031","section":"IV. Price-Adjustment Process","anchor_text":"ENERGY TRADING 2031 al- The process is scalable, since, at each iteration, only the lowest price rem","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The process is scalable, since, at each iteration, only the lowest price remaining upstream contract and highest price remaining downstream need to be considered, and the number of available contracts is reduced. ... The price-adjustment process is completed for the forward and real-time markets, so that in each market, the agents agree on a network of contracts which none of them wish to mutually deviate from. The price-adjustment process is constructed with buyers making progressively higher offers for trades to potential sellers, and sellers choosing to accept or reject the offers they receive."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-4a31f0141b-p08-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":8,"printed_page":"2033","section":"VI. Conclusion","anchor_text":"ers market uncertainty. Utility-maximising preferences for real- are time contracts and forward cont","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"A new scalable market design for P2P energy trading has been presented, using bilateral contract networks. The design includes forward and real-time markets and incorporates important characteristics particular to energy trading, including upstream-downstream energy balance and forward market uncertainty. Utility-maximising preferences for real-time contracts and forward contracts have been presented for different types of electricity market participants. It has been shown that these preferences satisfy full substitutability conditions, which ensures a distributed price-adjustment process can be used to find an agreed network of contracts that the agents do not wish to mutually deviate from."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"matching","context_text":"Contract-network topology used in case studies A and B. | Forward and real-time bilateral P2P markets; agents selecting contracts with potential counterparties. | Individual contract selection during each iteration of the forward and real-time price-adjustment process. | Initialization of the price-adjustment process in each forward and real-time market; all agents. | Permitted extensions of the proposed bilateral P2P methodology beyond the illustrated case-study topology. | Potential counterparty relationships in the forward and real-time bilateral contract networks.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g02-E15","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E26"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"matching.counterparties","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E19","v141-b-g02-E26"]},"paper_scope_note":"Initialization, conditional price adjustment after offer rejection, and the final stable contract are different stages; fully substitutable preferences are a stability condition, and the cycle in the original graph is not a direct equivalence relation."}});
